    "text": "Zero one, zero one, everything resolves, interpairs, except me. Two bodies bending space and symmetry, perfect ellipsis drawn so easily. Every streetlight hums in harmony, paired reflections staring back at me. Table set for two, tickets printed clean, every algorithm knows what. I have never been, I drift between the numbers, never quite assigned. An unpaired remainder in a system well defined, you orbit your line. Like gravity was always kind to signals intertwined, while I flicker out of time. Zero looking for one, but I'm neither never done just noise between the lines. Binary logic built into the walls, left side, right side, rise and fall. Magnetic poles that always choose, attract, repel, no room to lose. North, south, without a doubt, everything knows what it's about. Meanwhile, I'm, ba, ba, ba, compass spinning in a room with no field. Trying to feel what everyone else seems, pre-wired to feel. Even silence comes into, echo answering what it knew. But my voice just dissipates before it can be returned to you. Orbit you align, code it deep in your design. Two currents intertwined, close circuits every time. Zero reaching for one, but I glitch before become undefined. In a binary star system, everything makes sense. Two masses, locked in motion, each shaping the other's path, predictable, beautiful, inevitable. But introduce a third, and suddenly, nothing resolves. I am that third body, not enough to belong too much to ignore. I watch the pairs like constellations, perfect in their repetitions. Every orbit writes a story, balanced, held in quite glory. And I try to map my place, and they're synchronized embrace, but my trajectory just breaks. Every pattern I can trace, maybe I'm not meant to bind. To a single mirrored mine, maybe I'm the shifting frame, but no system can contain you. Orbit you align, but your gravity's not mine too. Signals intertwined, I dissolve between the signs. Zero never was a one, still the code keeps running on, and I'm somewhere in the soul. Zero one, zero one, the universe refers, a pair, but I remain unresolved. A third body, drifting through perfect systems that were never designed for me. A third body, drifting through perfect systems that were never designed for me.",
